   "text": {
    "L1": "Junk food may taste good, but it has a lot of salt, sugar or fat and little of what the body needs.",
    "L2": "Chips, cold drinks and instant noodles are junk food; roasted chana, bananas and sprouts chaat are healthier choices.",
    "L3": "It is fine once in a while, but eating junk food often can cause weight gain, tooth decay, low energy and illness.",
    "L4": "A packet's ingredients are listed with the biggest amount first, so read the label instead of trusting pictures or words like healthy.",
    "L5": "This drink lists water, sugar and only twelve percent fruit pulp, so it is mostly water and sugar.",
    "L6": "Fresh fruit is better than packaged juice because it has fibre and no added sugar.",
    "L7": "A cold drink has about eight teaspoons of added sugar, while plain milk and a fresh orange have none.",
    "L8": "Now use the label clue: choose the food that is mostly water and sugar."
   },
